\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Core Principle
\f1\b0 \
Treat a long PDF/book/report as a 
\f0\b reviewable dossier
\f1\b0 , not a single text blob. The system should move from:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 document 
\f3 \uc0\u8594 
\f2  page map 
\f3 \uc0\u8594 
\f2  structural sections 
\f3 \uc0\u8594 
\f2  evidence spans 
\f3 \uc0\u8594 
\f2  AI proposals 
\f3 \uc0\u8594 
\f2  researcher decisions 
\f3 \uc0\u8594 
\f2  public outputs
\f1\fs24 \
The AI should never \'93finish\'94 the document. It should create 
\f0\b ranked, evidence-linked proposals
\f1\b0  that the researcher can accept, edit, merge, reject, defer, or send for reanalysis.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Review Objects
\f1\b0 \
You need review states at several levels, because \'93reviewed document\'94 is too vague.\

